context and perform multiple operations\n   117→\n   118→## Tech Stack\n   119→\n   120→- **Runtime**: Bun\n   121→- **Language**: TypeScript\n   122→- **UI Framework**: React\n   123→- **AI Model**: Claude (Anthropic)\n   124→- **Protocol**: WebSocket + WebMCP\n   125→- **Build Tool**: Bun bundler\n   126→\n   127→## Usage Examples\n   128→\n   129→### Floating AI Chat (Recommended)\n   130→\n   131→The easiest way to add AI capabilities is using the built-in floating chat UI:\n   132→\n   133→```tsx\n   134→import { UseAIProvider } from '@use-ai/client';\n   135→import App from './App';\n   136→import { todoTools } from './tools';\n   137→\n   138→<UseAIProvider\n   139→  serverUrl=\"ws://localhost:8080\"\n   140→  showFloatingChat={true}\n   141→  globalTools={todoTools}\n   142→>\n   143→  <App />\n   144→</UseAIProvider>\n   145→```\n   146→\n   147→This displays a floating \"AI\" button in the bottom-right corner. Users can click it to open a chat interface and interact with your app using natural language.\n   148→\n   149→### Programmatic API\n   150→\n   151→For custom UI implementations:\n   152→\n   153→```tsx\n   154→import { UseAIProvider, useAI } from '@use-ai/client';\n   155→\n   156→function App() {\n   157→  const { response, loading, generate } = useAI({\n   158→    tools: {\n   159→      addTodo: {\n   160→        fn: (input) => addTodo(input.text),\n   161→        config: {\n   162→          description: 'Add a new todo item',\n   163→          parameters: {\n   164→            text: { type: 'string', required: true }\n   165→          }\n   166→        }\n   167→      }\n   168→    }\n   169→  });\n   170→\n   171→  return (\n   172→    <div>\n   173→      <button onClick={() => generate('Add a todo for grocery shopping')}>\n   174→        Ask AI\n   175→      </button>\n   176→      {response && <p>{response}</p>}\n   177→    </div>\n   178→  );\n   179→}\n   180→\n   181→<UseAIProvider serverUrl=\"ws://localhost:8080\">\n   182→  <App />\n   